{"id": "EUVD-2026-82294", "enisaUuid": "61ea7c62-32dc-37bf-9d0e-bef38d6c51a8", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ncxl/mbox: Clamp mailbox output allocation to the payload size\n\nCXL_MEM_SEND_COMMAND bounds the user's in.size to the mailbox payload\nsize but leaves out.size unbounded, then cxl_mbox_cmd_ctor() calls\nkvzalloc(out.size). A large out.size drives a huge allocation, above\nINT_MAX it WARNs and taints, and with panic_on_warn=1 it panics.\n\nThe transport __cxl_pci_mbox_send_cmd() already clamps the response copy\nto min(out.size, payload_size, device len), so the output buffer is\nnever written beyond payload_size. Clamp the allocation to payload_size\ntoo, matching the RAW path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:12:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2d40574b9b272ade32d0d77b140d990e7547f5f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5d2bbf0300f46307948864fbb97bce5097f4fe2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31d4841eca7c4b75751ca96d24339e19303337f2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b4e11c731d6bee3b87315e055a1ca417c92dc1fc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a13db9f899d149c3aab24abcb668121cfda5a4f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93186", "GHSA-4xf9-vh86-48mc"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "146d4db2-4384-303b-9fb0-3bcae4d94283", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "583fa5e71caeb79e04e477e9837e2f7fa53b71e4 <b4e11c731d6bee3b87315e055a1ca417c92dc1fc"}, {"id": "2bf61f1f-d999-37ce-bdb3-b1de8b0f65d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "39bf5111-c77e-3280-a3e4-ab8413e85e36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4c0d0d07-c638-316d-a22e-7b07d8b55760", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "668b58c6-7b8d-364c-9b52-7208a6994f87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.12"}, {"id": "6c508eef-ce39-3e0d-b387-43baa4cf031c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "8382cee9-14de-34e6-9675-e86273ff0867", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8c312668-1d92-3575-8489-c7e29f37697a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "583fa5e71caeb79e04e477e9837e2f7fa53b71e4 <31d4841eca7c4b75751ca96d24339e19303337f2"}, {"id": "8e2b6003-6047-318a-807b-877e94458b55", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "583fa5e71caeb79e04e477e9837e2f7fa53b71e4 <f5d2bbf0300f46307948864fbb97bce5097f4fe2"}, {"id": "a113464d-3538-3640-804c-e71525d39219", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "583fa5e71caeb79e04e477e9837e2f7fa53b71e4 <8a13db9f899d149c3aab24abcb668121cfda5a4f"}, {"id": "ccfaa404-1898-3142-9cbc-2bcf67c31ca3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "583fa5e71caeb79e04e477e9837e2f7fa53b71e4 <d2d40574b9b272ade32d0d77b140d990e7547f5f"}, {"id": "e2f2fa50-9e34-336b-adb7-dfb6c4e688d3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4bf53914-ef76-3536-8e25-5bd9d618c2d8", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}